npx lint-staged

# Type-check with the same compiler the build uses. `tsc` is TypeScript 7
# (@typescript/native) — the compiler that actually builds this project — not
# the `tsc6` that exists only so typescript-eslint has the older compiler API
# (see CONTRIBUTING, "Why are there two TypeScript packages?"). Checking with a
# different compiler than the build would be worse than not checking at all: a
# diagnostic one reports and the other accepts is a false alarm at the worst
# possible moment.
#
# Whole project, not just the staged files: a change in one file breaking
# another is exactly what this is here to catch. Expect it to add a few seconds
# to every commit — `git commit --no-verify` when you knowingly want to land
# something that does not compile yet.
npx tsc --noEmit
